  message: "CLOSED done, 2026-09-25 (P2 review, dev e4a47383ab). DONE-AND-NEVER-CLOSED: fixed by 95cc1521b4 (2026-08-31, \"fix(taint): a launch that returns the child's bytes is a transfer (INV-lozat)\"). That commit rows 18 content-returning launch symbols in 8 languages as ipc_recv, `simultaneous: true`, so the launch keeps its subprocess sink AND gains the untrusted-input source half this row said the WI-jupaf re-key had left unlabelled.\n\nEVIDENCE through the production catalogue loader (`taint.load_full_taint_catalog()`), for the row's named primitives:\n  erlang SOURCE  os:cmd       taint_label=untrusted_input, return_tainted=True, source_boundary=ipc_recv\n  erlang SINK    os:cmd       zone=subprocess   (the re-key's sink, kept, as the row asked)\n  elixir SOURCE  System.cmd, os.cmd   (same shape)\n  elixir SINK    System.cmd, os.cmd, erlang.open_port   zone=subprocess\nSo `Data = os:cmd(\"curl https://attacker.example\")` now yields an untrusted_input source, and the row's \"nothing labels it\" no longer holds. The old wrong label (host_secret via env_read) stays gone.\n\nNOT ASSERTED / NOT DONE HERE:\n- `erlang:open_port/2` is a SINK but NOT a source. It returns a port HANDLE, not the child's bytes (the data arrives later as messages). That is the handle-returning shape the INV-lozat commit explicitly left to a separate filing, not this row's content-returning case.\n- No end-to-end verify-claims run on an erlang fixture was made for this closure. The evidence is the production loader's merged catalogue, not a flow verdict."  # 2d69
